    "Cyclosporiasis — TLCHD noon dashboard July 31 is the definitive epidemiological test: today is the last day a July 17 Taylor Farms exposure can produce a new confirmed case under the 14-day maximum incubation period; Lucas County three-day rolling average (July 28: 24, July 29: 10, July 30: 11) is the strongest sustained deceleration since the peak; if today's count holds near single digits the primary outbreak is functionally closed; the unresolved second unnamed cluster (72 cases, food vehicle unknown, active FDA investigation) becomes the only open risk for August.",
    "Gordie Howe Bridge — Day 5 of commercial operations; first-week aggregate commercial vehicle crossing data from WDBA/CBSA still not published; commercial carrier uptake is expected to build as fleets complete required documentation; pedestrian and cyclist pathway opens August 5 at 8 a.m. (toll-free, passport required) — the only legal pedestrian/bike border crossing between Michigan and Canada; volume data is the leading metric for whether the I-75 corridor shift Toledo EDOs have marketed is materializing.",
    "Toledo Jeep Fest — August 6–9 (6 days away); 100K+ attendees expected downtown for the 10th festival and 85th Jeep anniversary; city road closure and logistics announcement not yet published (2025 equivalent appeared July 28, 2025); imminent release expected from toledo.oh.gov.",
    "Lucas County budget — 13% reduction directive covers all departments for 2027 budgets; $27M structural gap driven by federal SNAP cuts (50% federal administrative cost share eliminated); no agency-level response proposals or commission hearings have been announced yet; watch for department submissions and any specific service-reduction proposals.",
